WEBVTT

1
00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.059
She's tougher than she looks.

2
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:29.083
She is training
to be a Jedi after all.

3
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.018
A rookie who drops
her own lightsaber. but still. A Jedi.

4
00:01:34.042 --> 00:01:37.167
Well. she was carrying
more than one.

5
00:01:38.708 --> 00:01:40.726
What do you think her next move will be?

6
00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:45.184
Jedi love to make a show
of helping the innocent.

7
00:01:45.208 --> 00:01:47.268
I doubt she'll fight back.

8
00:01:47.292 --> 00:01:49.083
She'll just keep running.

9
00:01:50.208 --> 00:01:53.601
She can run all she wants.
but she won't escape.

10
00:01:53.625 --> 00:01:55.934
The Jedi are fools.

11
00:01:55.958 --> 00:01:58.667
Always making the same mistakes.

12
00:02:15.208 --> 00:02:19.166
My Lord. repairs
on the kyber cannon have been completed.

13
00:02:21.792 --> 00:02:26.042
I assume all it needs now
is a giant kyber crystal.

14
00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:49.041
I beg you. please stay back.

15
00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:55.582
Eesha?

16
00:02:58.542 --> 00:03:00.875
Eesha's been taken hostage?

17
00:03:01.583 --> 00:03:04.417
No...

18
00:03:30.083 --> 00:03:32.667
Four-Nines. have you found
Nawaam's destination yet?

19
00:03:36.292 --> 00:03:37.707
Hy Izlan?

20
00:03:39.125 --> 00:03:41.750
He must be after
the Sacred Crystal in the Aerial Temple.

21
00:03:45.375 --> 00:03:47.332
Make sure that Ethan knows about this.

22
00:04:04.542 --> 00:04:05.542
What is it?

23
00:04:06.833 --> 00:04:08.226
Huh?

24
00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:11.375
Look. Just in from Four-Nines.

25
00:04:13.625 --> 00:04:14.625
This can't be right!

26
00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:45.583
You're the ones. aren't you?
Who took my father...

27
00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:54.476
Are you going to kill me now?

28
00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:56.875
That's not for us to decide.

29
00:05:06.958 --> 00:05:10.684
Hey. hey. hey. hey!
That'd be a waste. don't you think?

30
00:05:10.708 --> 00:05:13.059
They still might be of some use to us.

31
00:05:13.083 --> 00:05:15.809
It'll make more sense to bring
at least one of them along.

32
00:05:15.833 --> 00:05:17.143
Don't you dare!

33
00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:19.268
Why bother?

34
00:05:19.292 --> 00:05:21.518
It's too much work for too little payoff.

35
00:05:21.542 --> 00:05:23.184
Fine.

36
00:05:23.208 --> 00:05:25.143
But you've gotta admit.

37
00:05:25.167 --> 00:05:27.184
Credits are still credits. though.

38
00:05:27.208 --> 00:05:28.624
Am I right?

39
00:05:41.583 --> 00:05:45.166
Make yourself scarce
before he changes his mind.

40
00:06:11.792 --> 00:06:14.083
Kara!

41
00:06:45.125 --> 00:06:47.351
Are you taking me to Nawaam?

42
00:06:47.375 --> 00:06:49.976
Not yet. Got a little detour.

43
00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.518
We're headed to recapture Zhima.

44
00:06:52.542 --> 00:06:53.601
Father?

45
00:06:53.625 --> 00:06:58.333
Word is. he went on a bit
of a rampage on one of Nawaam's outposts.

46
00:06:58.875 --> 00:07:01.583
Wiped the whole place out by himself.

47
00:07:02.708 --> 00:07:05.351
Jedi... Sith... There's no difference.

48
00:07:05.375 --> 00:07:08.226
They both leave behind
the same trail of destruction.

49
00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:11.268
No. you're wrong!
The Jedi fight in the name of justice.

50
00:07:11.292 --> 00:07:12.851
Let me ask you this.

51
00:07:12.875 --> 00:07:15.749
How many people have you killed
for the sake of justice?

52
00:07:20.417 --> 00:07:22.018
Power is power.

53
00:07:22.042 --> 00:07:23.601
You're strong. or you're weak.

54
00:07:23.625 --> 00:07:25.351
That's all there is to it.

55
00:07:25.375 --> 00:07:28.250
It's got nothing to do
with justice or evil.

56
00:07:30.208 --> 00:07:32.768
So that's it then?
You think power is all that matters?

57
00:07:32.792 --> 00:07:35.143
Take a good look
at yourself right now.

58
00:07:35.167 --> 00:07:37.768
What good has your righteousness done you?

59
00:07:37.792 --> 00:07:39.184
Give it a rest.

60
00:07:39.208 --> 00:07:42.208
Quit obsessing
about archaic Jedi teachings.

61
00:07:43.167 --> 00:07:46.851
You know. if you did.
you might actually be a match for us.

62
00:07:46.875 --> 00:07:49.226
Are you planning on fighting me?

63
00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:52.976
There's nothing I enjoy more
than fighting a strong enemy.

64
00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:56.434
That's why I chose
this line of work. after all.

65
00:07:56.458 --> 00:08:01.042
And that is also why you turned out
to be such a disappointment.

66
00:08:03.958 --> 00:08:07.292
<i>What does he mean by that?</i>

67
00:08:18.625 --> 00:08:21.750
I've done my best
to follow all the Jedi teachings.

68
00:08:22.875 --> 00:08:25.958
But I don't know
what I'm doing anymore.

69
00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:33.000
What's wrong. Kara?

70
00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:38.208
Juro!

71
00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:44.976
I gave in to the dark side.

72
00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.375
I failed you.

73
00:08:47.208 --> 00:08:50.393
Kara. why would you think
something like that?

74
00:08:50.417 --> 00:08:53.958
Because when it mattered.
I couldn't control my feelings.

75
00:08:55.375 --> 00:08:58.083
And then my lightsaber. it turned red.

76
00:09:01.625 --> 00:09:04.434
All those lightsabers your father forged.

77
00:09:04.458 --> 00:09:07.768
they have the ability to reflect
the wielder's thoughts and emotions.

78
00:09:07.792 --> 00:09:09.393
For example.

79
00:09:09.417 --> 00:09:14.726
the color red symbolizes
the feelings of rage. hatred and fear.

80
00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:17.809
Being a Jedi doesn't mean
not having these feelings.

81
00:09:17.833 --> 00:09:20.684
As long as you
do not let them control you.

82
00:09:20.708 --> 00:09:23.042
then you will not succumb
to the dark side.

83
00:09:24.708 --> 00:09:26.958
But I... I killed all of those people...

84
00:09:27.667 --> 00:09:30.559
And I'm afraid of it happening again.

85
00:09:30.583 --> 00:09:31.934
I can't fight anymore.

86
00:09:31.958 --> 00:09:33.333
I just can't risk it.

87
00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:37.184
So. when those in need
come seeking your help.

88
00:09:37.208 --> 00:09:38.851
will you refuse to assist them?

89
00:09:38.875 --> 00:09:41.500
But what am I supposed to do?

90
00:09:42.958 --> 00:09:47.458
Unfortunately. that is a question
I do not have the answer to.

91
00:09:48.625 --> 00:09:52.167
If even you don't know what to do.
then how am I supposed to?

92
00:09:53.417 --> 00:09:55.226
Trust in the Force.

93
00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:59.750
And if you do. you will be naturally
guided to the answer you seek.

94
00:10:04.333 --> 00:10:07.976
The Force flows through
every single living thing.

95
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:11.059
So long as we follow
wherever it guides us.

96
00:10:11.083 --> 00:10:13.518
we will always find our true path.

97
00:10:13.542 --> 00:10:18.476
Kara. I hope that whatever answer
that you do find

98
00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:21.226
will lead you to a new solution

99
00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:24.833
that is different
from our old way of life.

100
00:10:26.583 --> 00:10:28.333
Juro!

101
00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:38.750
Juro...

102
00:11:10.875 --> 00:11:12.184
<i>Have you found anything?</i>

103
00:11:12.208 --> 00:11:14.143
<i>We need to know where he's going.</i>

104
00:11:14.167 --> 00:11:15.708
<i>Understood?</i>

105
00:11:29.125 --> 00:11:32.059
He caused
all of this destruction.

106
00:11:32.083 --> 00:11:35.018
<i>and yet. didn't take a single life.</i>

107
00:11:35.042 --> 00:11:36.476
<i>Why go to the trouble?</i>

108
00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:38.476
<i>Must be on some mercy kick.</i>

109
00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:40.393
<i>- Idiot.
- Yup.</i>

110
00:11:40.417 --> 00:11:42.917
<i>Hurry up and get to the control room
to look for clues.</i>

111
00:11:43.958 --> 00:11:45.875
Be safe. Father.

112
00:11:49.417 --> 00:11:50.542
<i>Find anything?</i>

113
00:11:52.250 --> 00:11:55.374
There are signs
of data being accessed.

114
00:11:56.458 --> 00:11:59.976
Ah. He's going after Nawaam.

115
00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.851
<i>By himself?</i>

116
00:12:01.875 --> 00:12:03.893
<i>Typical Jedi.</i>

117
00:12:03.917 --> 00:12:06.184
<i>What do we do now?</i>

118
00:12:06.208 --> 00:12:09.268
Well. at this rate.
he's going to get to Nawaam

119
00:12:09.292 --> 00:12:11.851
before we have a chance to intercept him.

120
00:12:11.875 --> 00:12:14.601
<i>If he does.
then we won't be able to take him in.</i>

121
00:12:14.625 --> 00:12:16.809
<i>which means we won't get paid.</i>

122
00:12:16.833 --> 00:12:19.351
<i>All this will have been for nothing.</i>

123
00:12:19.375 --> 00:12:21.309
We can't have that. now. can we?

124
00:12:21.333 --> 00:12:24.542
We have no choice but to use the girl
to lure Zhima out.

125
00:12:25.375 --> 00:12:28.518
Normally. I'd complain
that we're using the same trick twice.

126
00:12:28.542 --> 00:12:30.893
but for once. I agree with you.

127
00:12:30.917 --> 00:12:32.458
<i>Their dirty little tricks...</i>

128
00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:37.226
They think they can use me
so they can set a trap for my father.

129
00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:39.499
Think again!

130
00:12:58.583 --> 00:13:00.583
Hmm?

131
00:13:01.625 --> 00:13:02.874
What?

132
00:13:08.917 --> 00:13:10.792
I won't let you touch my father!

133
00:13:11.542 --> 00:13:14.726
I'm afraid Gennoh has his heart set
on having a rematch with him.

134
00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:15.809
I don't care!

135
00:13:15.833 --> 00:13:18.934
You were supposed to be bait.
but that's no longer an option.

136
00:13:18.958 --> 00:13:20.458
Time to die.

137
00:13:29.458 --> 00:13:30.684
<i>Smoke?</i>

138
00:13:30.708 --> 00:13:32.292
<i>No. wait. Mist.</i>

139
00:13:33.333 --> 00:13:35.750
How good a fighter are you?

140
00:13:36.542 --> 00:13:39.624
Does the Force actually guide you?

141
00:13:45.792 --> 00:13:49.309
I'd expect
nothing less from a Jedi.

142
00:13:49.333 --> 00:13:52.500
But how long
will you be able to keep evading?

143
00:14:28.208 --> 00:14:31.101
Eht. how do you expect me
to back you up?

144
00:14:31.125 --> 00:14:32.916
<i>Just shut up and watch.</i>

145
00:14:47.417 --> 00:14:50.268
That lightsaber makes you look
just like a Sith.

146
00:14:50.292 --> 00:14:51.541
Shut up!

147
00:14:53.583 --> 00:14:57.417
But then again. so does the way
you let your emotions control your blade.

148
00:15:04.625 --> 00:15:05.625
Shut up!

149
00:15:07.542 --> 00:15:08.542
Shut up!

150
00:15:09.292 --> 00:15:10.917
Shut...

151
00:15:12.917 --> 00:15:15.457
Stop hiding! Coward!

152
00:15:19.625 --> 00:15:21.851
<i>Do not let your emotions
overtake you.</i>

153
00:15:21.875 --> 00:15:24.250
<i>Focus on the Force. Let it guide you.</i>

154
00:15:24.958 --> 00:15:26.291
Juro...

155
00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:45.999
How did she...

156
00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:55.042
All right. then...

157
00:15:58.625 --> 00:16:00.667
She's reacting
faster than before.

158
00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:07.143
Turning off your saber. huh?

159
00:16:07.167 --> 00:16:09.893
If you think that's going to make it
harder for me to see you.

160
00:16:09.917 --> 00:16:11.916
I'm afraid you're sorely mistaken.

161
00:16:24.125 --> 00:16:25.458
When did she draw her weapon?

162
00:16:26.375 --> 00:16:27.792
{\an8}After the beam fired?

163
00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:32.184
Did she just predict
where the beams will be coming from?

164
00:16:32.208 --> 00:16:34.559
Is she reading Eht's mind?

165
00:16:34.583 --> 00:16:35.583
No...

166
00:16:36.375 --> 00:16:39.042
{\an8}What is this?

167
00:16:53.833 --> 00:16:56.458
{\an8}Wait. Can she see them?

168
00:16:58.375 --> 00:17:00.333
A silver lightsaber?

169
00:17:00.917 --> 00:17:02.292
You...

170
00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:17.351
Once I figured it out.
I knew it was another dirty trick.

171
00:17:17.375 --> 00:17:19.125
You think this is a joke?

172
00:17:32.583 --> 00:17:35.291
Never revealing
your finishing move...

173
00:17:36.375 --> 00:17:39.292
That's a Jedi for you.

174
00:17:45.958 --> 00:17:48.292
More blood. I have more blood on my hands.

175
00:17:51.375 --> 00:17:54.625
This saber...
It's the same color as Nawaam's.

176
00:17:55.667 --> 00:17:56.667
That means...

177
00:18:04.333 --> 00:18:07.167
Were you fighting
without having any thoughts?

178
00:18:08.208 --> 00:18:09.208
Yikes.

179
00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:25.434
If I can't read your next move.
I can't risk closing the gap.

180
00:18:25.458 --> 00:18:29.167
But... I can do this!

181
00:18:41.583 --> 00:18:43.125
Do not play with me!

182
00:18:56.083 --> 00:18:57.500
Aren't you gonna kill me?

183
00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:03.333
If possible.
I'd rather not take any more lives.

184
00:19:04.625 --> 00:19:06.309
Naive of me. huh?

185
00:19:06.333 --> 00:19:09.393
Yeah. I'd say so.

186
00:19:09.417 --> 00:19:10.726
Even so.

187
00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:13.208
this means that from now on
your life belongs to me.

188
00:19:15.625 --> 00:19:18.059
You will serve me
and follow the orders I give you.

189
00:19:18.083 --> 00:19:19.143
Huh?

190
00:19:19.167 --> 00:19:20.167
Understood?

191
00:19:25.167 --> 00:19:27.309
All right. fine.

192
00:19:27.333 --> 00:19:30.999
I guess I'll be calling you
Master from now on.

193
00:19:47.958 --> 00:19:49.851
Were the two of you friends?

194
00:19:49.875 --> 00:19:51.750
We worked together a long time.

195
00:19:53.083 --> 00:19:55.726
He was a real piece of work.

196
00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:58.833
But he treated his fellow hunters well.

197
00:20:00.958 --> 00:20:02.684
You don't have to worry.

198
00:20:02.708 --> 00:20:06.309
In this line of work.
trading lives is part of the game.

199
00:20:06.333 --> 00:20:08.167
So. no hard feelings.

200
00:20:15.583 --> 00:20:16.583
Here.

201
00:20:18.083 --> 00:20:19.601
What's this?

202
00:20:19.625 --> 00:20:21.934
You're gonna need it
if you're helping me.

203
00:20:21.958 --> 00:20:24.500
Did I forget to mention.
you work for me now?

204
00:20:28.042 --> 00:20:30.292
If you say so. But you better pay me well.

205
00:20:32.125 --> 00:20:35.143
You said you liked fighting
strong enemies. didn't you?

206
00:20:35.167 --> 00:20:36.476
Well. if you come with me.

207
00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:39.559
then I promise.
you'll face a lot of strong enemies.

208
00:20:39.583 --> 00:20:41.250
You mean Nawaam's army?

209
00:20:42.208 --> 00:20:45.268
Well. that's a guaranteed death sentence.

210
00:20:45.292 --> 00:20:46.351
Probably.

211
00:20:46.375 --> 00:20:49.726
But you'll be able to fight
on the side of justice.

212
00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:52.268
There we go. right on cue.

213
00:20:52.292 --> 00:20:54.333
Again. with the Jedi teachings.

214
00:20:55.708 --> 00:21:00.351
No. This has nothing to do
with rules or teachings.

215
00:21:00.375 --> 00:21:02.143
It's something that must be done.

216
00:21:02.167 --> 00:21:03.792
This is my decision.

217
00:21:05.625 --> 00:21:06.625
Hmm.

218
00:21:16.042 --> 00:21:18.917
You see? I knew I made the right choice.

219
00:21:20.125 --> 00:21:21.957
Seriously?
